---
description: Core rules for every task in the Rewind repo
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md` before starting. It is the source of truth for workflow, stack and code rules.
- If you were asked to do "Part N" of an issue, do only that part. Follow its Requirements, run its Checks, use its commit message. Push to the existing PR branch. Never open a second PR.
- Read the GitHub issue fully. Follow its "Scope" and "Definition of done" sections exactly.
- Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before touching `packages/`.
- One issue = one branch = one PR. Branch name `day-XX/short-name`. PR title `[Day XX] ...`. PR body has `Closes #N`.
- Test-first inside every part: a `test(...)` commit with tests and stubs, then the implementation commit. Never weaken tests from the test commit.
- Also read `.cursor/rules/90-lessons.mdc` before you start.
- Run `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build` before pushing. All must pass.
- Never skip or delete tests. Never weaken CI.
- The recorder must never throw into the host app. Wrap risky code.
- Mask sensitive input by default.
- Explain every non-obvious decision in the PR description in plain English. Important ones also get an ADR in `docs/decisions/`.
